y assessed."],"questionId":"cnm_p211_q3","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p210","cnm_p110","cnm_p039","cnm_p083"],"id":"proportion-equation","label":"Use the supplied proportion","methodDirectNodeIds":{"proportion-equation":["cnm_p211"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p211","cnm_p210","cnm_p110","cnm_p039","cnm_p083"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":6,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: 18","reason":"Label the lower vertices A and B, the top vertex C, side points D on AC and E on BC, and the crossing P. Equal area-7 triangles give AP=PE, while DP:PB=3:7. Put u=[CPE] and v=[CPD]. Then u=v+3 and (u+7)/v=7/3. Solving gives v=15/2 and u=21/2, so the shaded area is u+v=18.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2006_AMC_10B_Q23","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_112","cnm_055","cnm_p210"],"id":"equal-areas-and-median","label":"Equal areas reveal a midpoint","methodDirectNodeIds":{"equal-areas-and-median":["cnm_p148","cnm_p150","cnm_113","cnm_042"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p148","cnm_p150","cnm_113","cnm_042","cnm_112","cnm_055","cnm_p210"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":6,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 10/91","reason":"Extend AG to meet line CD at H beyond C. Similarity gives CH=5/3, hence FH=14/3. Since AE=4 and CF=3, EP/EF=4/(4+3)=4/7. Similarly, EQ/EF=4/(4+14/3)=6/13. Thus PQ/EF=4/7-6/13=10/91.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2016_AMC_10B_Q19","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_069","cnm_063","cnm_055","cnm_p210"],"id":"solution:similar-triangle-ratios:3decb046f863","label":"Locate the intersections using similar triangles","methodDirectNodeIds":{"similar-triangle-ratios":["cnm_268","cnm_271","cnm_272"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_268","cnm_271","cnm_272","cnm_069","cnm_063","cnm_055","cnm_p210"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_082","cnm_089","cnm